"""Capture existing app text and reproducible, verse-specific art prompts."""
import json,sqlite3
from pathlib import Path

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
OUT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
con=sqlite3.connect('file:'+str(ROOT/'backend/app.db')+'?mode=ro',uri=True);con.row_factory=sqlite3.Row
raw=[dict(r) for r in con.execute("SELECT verse_uid,source_ref,devanagari,iast,translation_en,translation_hi FROM shlokas WHERE source_ref LIKE 'Īśopaniṣad %'")]
best={}
for row in raw:
 n=int(row['source_ref'].rsplit(' ',1)[1]);previous=best.get(n)
 if previous is None or len(row['devanagari'])>len(previous['devanagari']):best[n]=row
assert sorted(best)==list(range(1,19))
verses=[best[n] for n in range(1,19)]
(OUT/'verses.json').write_text(json.dumps(verses,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
scenes=[
 'A single continuous landscape of river, trees, grazing deer, a tiny village and distant mountains, all gently permeated by the same subtle golden daylight. A modest person receives a small bowl of fruit with open hands while leaving the abundance of the living world undisturbed. Evoke divine pervasion, enjoyment with relinquishment, and freedom from coveting; no anthropomorphic deity.',
 'A humble person working attentively in a small field and watering a sapling at dawn, with a mature tree nearby suggesting a long life of purposeful action. Open, unpossessive hands and quiet sustained work, no chains or trophies. Evoke acting throughout a hundred-year life without being bound by action.',
 'A solitary tiny traveler at the threshold of a sunless mist-covered valley, their face turned away from a small warm light behind them. Atmospheric indigo-gray darkness veils the landscape without horror. Symbolic spiritual blindness and forgetting the Self; no injury, death, corpse, self-harm, demons or punishment imagery.',
 'A still, clear pool at the center of a windswept landscape. Rushing clouds, moving grasses and birds suggest the swiftness of thought, while a single unwavering reflection of soft light remains still. Wind moves across water. Interpret the unmoving Self, swifter than thought, and Matarishvan sustaining activity; no human embodiment of the Self.',
 'A dewdrop on a leaf in the foreground reflecting the same far mountain and sky that extend behind it. A nearby quiet pond and distant moving clouds merge into one continuous atmosphere. Evoke the near and far, moving and unmoving, within and beyond; no separate collage panels.',
 'A peaceful person seated at the edge of a woodland clearing, with a deer, small birds, trees and other people sharing the same soft reflected light in a still pond. No central figure dominates the other beings. Evoke seeing all beings in the Self and the Self in all, without rejection or aversion.',
 'A person with a relaxed, quietly joyful expression among a small diverse gathering of people, a deer and birds beside a river; their many reflections meet in one unbroken expanse of water. An unobtrusive scene of unity dissolving sorrow and separation. No halos identifying any one human as the supreme Self.',
 'Pure, formless diffuse light permeates an ordered natural landscape of water, stone, growing plants, sky and stars fading into morning. No human or divine body at the center: brightness without physical form, purity, self-existence and an enduring order. Detailed natural watercolor rather than a geometric diagram.',
 'Two narrow footpaths disappear into the same deep twilight forest: on one side abandoned ritual implements without understanding, on the other an isolated closed manuscript without lived engagement. A small balanced open clearing remains possible between them. Symbolic caution about one-sided avidya and vidya, not a claim that learning or ritual is evil. No labels or moral caricatures.',
 'An elderly forest teacher speaks gently to two attentive pupils in a quiet grove. Beside one pupil rests a simple tool for practical work; beside the other an open palm-leaf manuscript. Both listen equally to a nuanced teaching about the different fruits of vidya and avidya. No written marks legible on the manuscript.',
 'A single traveler crosses a modest river footbridge while carrying a simple work tool and a closed palm-leaf manuscript together, with both hands balanced. The near bank has seasonal fallen leaves; the far bank holds enduring morning light. Symbolic integration of knowledge and action, crossing mortality toward the deathless; no literal supernatural portal.',
 'A misty grove of emerging shoots, mature trees and decaying wood, with one observer focused only on a single fallen branch and another focused only on a blooming tree; both lose sight of the whole living grove in deep twilight. Evoke the warning against exclusive fixation on the unmanifest or manifest, using an open-ended contemplative metaphor rather than a doctrinal diagram.',
 'A forest sage teaches a small pair of attentive pupils beside a seed, a growing sapling and an old fallen trunk, all belonging to one natural cycle. The teacher gestures openly toward the whole scene, explaining that manifestation and the unmanifest have different fruits. No invented deity or printed explanation.',
 'A quiet riverbank holds an old fallen tree nourishing a vigorous new sapling, with a modest person observing the single continuous life of the grove. Soft light beyond the river evokes what endures while forms arise and pass away. Symbolic understanding of arising and dissolution together, passing mortality toward the deathless; no resurrection or literal immortal body.',
 'A radiant golden sun disk partially veiled by a thin luminous sheet of cloud, with a narrow opening revealing clear white-gold light beyond. A small contemplative observer below looks upward with reverence. Evoke the golden covering over the face of truth and the prayer to Pushan to uncover it; no giant human face or text in the sun.',
 'Warm rays of the sun gather into a quiet clear center above a small contemplative figure in an open landscape. The person and the distant sunlight share a gentle continuous glow, expressing recognition rather than separation. Evoke the prayer to Pushan, the sun, to gather its rays and reveal the auspicious form, and recognition of unity. No anthropomorphic face inside the sun.',
 'A gentle breeze moves dry leaves over a small, cold, clean patch of pale ash near an extinguished ceremonial hearth. The open sky continues above a calm river; a faint trail of air is suggested only by moving leaves. Evoke breath returning to immortal air, the body to ashes, and remembrance of deeds, without depicting a dying person, corpse, cremation or distress.',
 'A small steady sacred flame beside a winding forest path lights the safe way toward a clear dawn horizon, while a crooked dark side-path fades into undergrowth. A modest traveler follows the well-lit path with folded hands. Evoke the closing prayer to Agni to guide by the good path and turn away crooked wrongdoing. No battle, no fiery destruction, no text.'
]
common=('Use case: illustration-story. One original high-resolution master painting for a Sanskrit reader, part of a consistent 18-image Ishopanishad series. '
 'Square 1:1 canvas, request 2048 by 2048 pixels or the highest supported square resolution. Refined traditional Indian watercolor and restrained gouache on warm ivory handmade paper; fine organic detail, quiet ochre, sage, dusty terracotta and muted indigo; dignified ancient Indian setting. '
 'Use one coherent scene, no collage. Main narrative subjects MUST fit inside the central 60 percent of the width and central 50 percent of the height; surround them with generous low-detail sky, paper atmosphere and ground. Avoid important faces, hands and narrative objects near edges. This single master will be used behind live text in portrait and landscape on phones and tablets; surrounding atmosphere can crop, the scene must remain intelligible when fitted without cropping. '
 'Do not draw any Sanskrit, Roman text, verse numbers, typography, frame, border, watermark, infographic, UI, or page decoration. Do not portray a formless teaching as a specific deity unless the verse explicitly invokes that deity. Interpretive devotional illustration, not a literal historical reconstruction. ')
jobs=[]
for n,(v,scene) in enumerate(zip(verses,scenes),1):
 jobs.append({'verse':n,'source_ref':v['source_ref'],'verse_uid':v['verse_uid'],'source_devanagari':v['devanagari'],'source_translation_en':v['translation_en'],'scene':scene,'prompt':common+'Verse-specific source meaning from the app: '+v['translation_en']+' Illustration: '+scene,'master':f'results/isha-art-20261016/masters/verse-{n:02d}.png','focal_point':[.5,.5],'safe_region':{'x':.08,'y':.08,'width':.84,'height':.84}})
(OUT/'generation-jobs.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Prepared',len(jobs),'verse-specific generation jobs; duplicate verse 1 resolved by fullest text.')
